              is a small-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functor"} continuous functor
              into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %p
              As before, for each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \downarrow R
              is locally small and small-complete. Moreover, it is easy to check that it is well-powered, and that the set of all objects of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \to R c_\alpha
              is a cogenerating set for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \downarrow R
            %p
              It then remains to prove that any locally small, small-complete, well-powered category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with a cogenerating set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{k_s: s \in S\}
              has an initial object. The initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              is constructed as the intersection = pullback of all subobjects of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_s k_s
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
