          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#InLocallyPresentableCategories In locally presentable categories
          %p
            The following is a counter-example, indicating the need for something more than just continuity to force a functor between locally presentable categories to be a right adjoint; as stated in theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjFuncTheoremForLocallyPresentableCats"}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For every infinite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+number"} cardinal number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\kappa
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+group"} simple group
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
